IP_NAME,Test_ID,Test_Name,Description,Preconditions,Steps,Expected_Result,Priority,Owner,Tags,Source_File,Source_URL
GPIO,GPIO_TP_001,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"Validate GPIO GP0 pin registers (8–27) for reset defaults and masked read/write behavior across multiple patterns.","- DUT powered and accessible\n- GPIO block clocked and mapped\n- Test framework initialized","1) Read each per-pin GPIO register (pins 8–27) using read mask and compare to documented reset default.\n2) For patterns {FFFFFFFF, AAAAAAAA, 55555555, F5F5F5F5, A5A5A5A5, FFFF0000}, write to each register using its write mask.\n3) Read back via read mask and compute expected: writable fields reflect pattern; non-writable fields remain default.\n4) Record mismatches and continue across all addresses and patterns.","PASS if all masked default reads match and all masked readbacks equal expected for every address and pattern; else FAIL.",NA,NA,"GPIO,registers,mask,defaults","program.c; test_define.c","https://github.com/titusbspgit/PSVValidation/tree/main/TestRepo/gpio/gpio_reg_wr_rd_test"
GPIO,GPIO_TP_002,test_gpio_negedge_intr_en,"Validate falling-edge (negedge) interrupt generation and handling per GPIO pad (32 pads), including enable, trigger, status check, and clear.","- GIC interrupt for GPIO group enabled (INT IDs 87/88 as applicable)\n- LSS SYSREG INTREN1 GPIOx interrupt enabled\n- GPIO per-pin control configured for input/edge detection","1) Enable INTREN1 bit for GPIO group interrupts.\n2) For each per-pin control register (pins 8–39), configure edge-detect and input mode as required.\n3) For each pad i, clear raw status via RAWSTCR1 and enable the corresponding bit in gp0_intr1_intr_en1.\n4) Drive external GPIO generator: set all high, then drive only pad i low to create a falling edge.\n5) Wait for ISR to fire within timeout.\n6) In ISR: verify per-pin status (gp0_gpio_i) indicates interrupt, group status (gp0_intr1_intr_sts1) has bit i set; clear per-pin raw via RAWSTCR1 and reconfigure pin if needed; confirm group status clears to 0; clear SYSREG RAWSTCR1 and GIC pending.","PASS if each pad triggers one falling-edge interrupt, group status reflects the pad, per-pin and group statuses clear correctly, and no timeouts occur; else FAIL.",NA,NA,"GPIO,interrupt,negedge","program.c; test_define.c","https://github.com/titusbspgit/PSVValidation/tree/main/TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_negedge_intr_en"
GPIO,GPIO_TP_003,test_gpio_pedge_all_pads_en,"Validate rising-edge (posedge) interrupt enable and service across all GPIO pads (32 pads): enable, trigger once, verify group status, and clear.","- GIC interrupt for GPIO group enabled\n- LSS SYSREG INTREN1 GPIOx interrupt enabled\n- GPIO IO control groups configured for input mode","1) Enable INTREN1 bit for GPIO group interrupts.\n2) For each per-pin control register (pins 8–39), set posedge enable bit.\n3) Set GPIO IO CTRL GROUP1..4 to input mode (as required).\n4) Enable gp0_intr1_intr_en1 for all pads.\n5) For each pad i, drive line low, arm wait flag, then drive high to generate a single rising edge; wait for ISR within timeout.\n6) In ISR: read group status (gp0_intr1_intr_sts1) and ensure non-zero; mask group enables; clear per-pin raw status by writing iclr bit; verify group status clears to 0; clear SYSREG RAWSTCR1; re-enable group interrupt and clear GIC pending.","PASS if each pad generates a rising-edge interrupt, ISR observes non-zero group status, per-pin raw clear succeeds (group status becomes 0), and SYSREG raw clear succeeds; else FAIL.",NA,NA,"GPIO,interrupt,posedge","program.c; test_define.c","https://github.com/titusbspgit/PSVValidation/tree/main/TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_pedge_all_pads_en"